          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Find the parity of the number of small squares in these grids:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.121,
            0.328,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 7 \\times 1 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (b) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 2 \\times 7 8"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (c) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 3 5 \\times 6 5 4"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.209,
            0.418,
            0.232
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Parity of Expressions"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.241,
            0.847,
            0.281
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider the algebraic expression: 3n + 4. For different values of n, the expression has different parity:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.288,
            0.811,
            0.403
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.186,
                0.288,
                0.811,
                0.403
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_table_5.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>n</td><td>Value of 3n + 4</td><td>Parity of the Value</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>13</td><td>odd</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>28</td><td>even</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>34</td><td>even</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.418,
            0.73,
            0.473
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Come up with an expression that always has even parity. Some examples are: 100p and 48w – 2. Try to find more."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.478,
            0.7,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Come up with expressions that always have odd parity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.518,
            0.847,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Come up with other expressions, like 3n + 4, which could have either odd or even parity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.575,
            0.848,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ The expression 6k + 2 evaluates to 8, 14, 20,... (for k = 1, 2, 3,...) — many even numbers are missing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.634,
            0.832,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Are there expressions using which we can list all the even numbers? "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " All even numbers have a factor 2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.694,
            0.785,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Are there expressions using which we can list all odd numbers?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.726,
            0.849,
            0.785
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We saw earlier how to express the n"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "th",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term of the sequence of multiples of 4, where n is the letter-number that denotes a position in the sequence (e.g., first, twenty third, hundred and seventeenth, etc.)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.788,
            0.848,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ What would be the n"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "th",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term for multiples of 2? Or, what is the n"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "th",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " even number?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.836,
            0.474,
            0.856
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us consider odd numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.861,
            0.469,
            0.884
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the 100th odd number?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.89,
            0.745,
            0.912
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To answer this question, consider the following question:"
